				"7B195200D9D3485B"
			]
			description: [
				"Cuts leave as hot as their section. Carbolic oil, creosote and vinegar come out too hot for any PVC pipe, and pitch is always kept warm. A Steel Condenser anywhere but beside a column cools hot cuts inline."
				""
				"Whatever escapes over the top hangs low as solvent vapour and flashes into flame at anything &eWarm&r or hotter. Mind your furnaces."
				""
				"&7JEI: the Cooling Hot Cuts tab.&r"
